  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> Vernier divisions are equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>49</mn></math> main scale divisions of a travelling microscope and one smallest reading of main scale is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mm</mi></math> the Vernier constant of travelling microscope is:",
    "image": null
